# IIML Semantic Checker

A comprehensive semantic analysis tool for the **Interactive Image Manipulation Language (IIML)**.

## Project Context

This semantic checker is part of the larger **IML (Image Manipulation Language)** compiler project and is located within the `src/iiml-semantic-check/` directory. It specifically focuses on analyzing IIML programs, integrating with the main compiler infrastructure in the parent `src/` directory and testing real IIML example programs from `../../examples/`.

## Project Structure

This semantic checker is organized to use source files from the parent `src` directory, avoiding code duplication:

```
src/iiml-semantic-check/
├── build.sh              # Build script (compiles from parent src/)
├── run_tests.sh          # Automated test runner with auto-build
├── READ.ME               # This documentation
└── tests/                # Test cases for IIML programs
    ├── test-01-undeclared-variable.iiml
    ├── test-02-variable-redeclaration.iiml
    ├── ...        
    ├── test-17-example-des-iiml-01.iiml    # Real IIML examples
    ├── test-18-example-min-iiml-01.iiml    # from ../../examples/
    └── test-19-example-min-iiml-02.iiml
```

**Note**: Generated directories (`classes/`, ANTLR files) are created during build and automatically cleaned up with the `--clean` flag.

## Quick Start

### One-Command Testing (Recommended)
```bash
./run_tests.sh --clean
```

This command will:
- **Auto-builds if needed** (detects missing compiled classes)
- Generates ANTLR files from `../GrammarIIML.g4`  
- Compiles all source files from parent `src/` directory
- Runs the complete test suite (**18 tests including real IIML examples**)
- **Automatically cleans up** all generated files and directories
- Leaves the workspace exactly as you found it

### Alternative Commands

#### Clean Build & Test
```bash
./build.sh --clean
```

#### Build Only
```bash
./build.sh
```

#### Test Only (auto-builds if needed)
```bash
./run_tests.sh
```

## Enhanced Features

### Core Semantic Analysis
- **Variable Declaration & Usage**: Validates number and list variable declarations with proper type checking
- **Type Compatibility**: Ensures type safety for assignments and arithmetic operations  
- **Scope Management**: Proper variable scoping for for-loops and nested contexts
- **List Validation**: Uses `ListType.hasUniformType()` for list type checking
- **Image & Figure Rules**: Validates image declarations and figure placement requirements
- **Figure Type Integration**: Uses Figure class instances (CircleFigure, RectangleFigure, etc.) for validation

### Quality of Life Features
- **Style Warnings**: Detects confusing variable names similar to reserved keywords
- **Unused Variable Detection**: Identifies declared but unused variables
- **Positive Value Validation**: Warns about negative dimensions in geometric figures
- **Comprehensive Error Reporting**: Clear error messages with line numbers and context
- **Analysis Summary**: Detailed statistics about variables, usage, and program structure

### Build System Enhancements
- **Auto-Build Detection**: Test runner automatically builds if classes are missing
- **Intelligent Cleanup**: Removes all generated files while preserving source code
- **Real Example Integration**: Tests include actual IIML examples from the project
- **Proper ANTLR Integration**: Uses system `antlr4` command for reliable file generation

## Test Coverage

Our test suite includes **18 tests** with 100% success rate:

### Error Detection Tests (8 tests)
- Undeclared variable usage
- Variable redeclaration  
- Type mismatches
- Invalid list operations
- Invalid for-loop constructs
- Missing image declarations
- Invalid arithmetic operations
- Non-uniform list types

### Valid Program Tests (7 tests)
- Basic valid programs
- Complex valid constructs
- Style warning detection
- Unused variable detection
- Multiple confusing names
- Assignment operations
- Negative dimension warnings

### Real IIML Example Tests (3 tests)
- **des-iiml-01.iiml**: Complex example with list of lists and for loops
- **min-iiml-01.iiml**: Simple image with rectangle placement
- **min-iiml-02.iiml**: Interactive example with user input and variables

These example tests validate the semantic checker against real-world IIML programs from the `../../examples/` directory.

## IIML Language Support

The semantic checker supports the following IIML constructs:

- **Variable Declarations**: `number x is 10`, `list of list of number centers is [[1,1], [3,3]]`
- **Assignments**: `x is 20`
- **Arithmetic**: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/` with proper type checking
- **Lists**: List literals, element access, uniform type validation, nested lists
- **Image Declaration**: `image size width by height background intensity`
- **Figure Placement**: `place circle/rect/cross/plus/line ...`
- **For Loops**: `for list item within listvar` with proper iterator scoping
- **Type Conversion**: `number(expression)`
- **Input**: `read "prompt"`

## Usage Examples

The test runner now auto-builds, so you can simply run tests directly. For manual testing:

```bash
# Run all tests with cleanup (recommended)
./run_tests.sh --clean

# Test specific IIML examples from the project
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck ../../examples/des-iiml-01.iiml
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck ../../examples/min-iiml-01.iiml
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck ../../examples/min-iiml-02.iiml

# Show help
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck --help

# Analyze specific test files
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck tests/test-09-valid-program.iiml
java -cp "/usr/local/lib/antlr-4.13.2-complete.jar:classes" IIMLSemanticCheck tests/test-17-example-des-iiml-01.iiml
```

## Implementation Notes

### Architecture
- Located in `src/iiml-semantic-check/` within the main project structure
- Uses source files from parent `src/` directory (no code duplication)
- Extends `GrammarIIMLBaseVisitor<Boolean>` for AST traversal
- Uses visitor pattern for semantic analysis
- Integrates with existing `ErrorHandling`, `NumberType`, `ListType`, and `Figure` classes

### Enhanced Integrations
- **Figure Type Validation**: Uses actual `Figure` class instances with a static map of valid figures
- **List Type Checking**: Leverages `ListType.hasUniformType()` for validation
- **Error Context**: All messages include precise line numbers and specific contexts
- **Real Example Testing**: Validates against actual IIML programs from the project

### File Organization
- **Source files**: Parent `src/` directory
- **Generated files**: Temporary directories created during build
- **Test files**: Local `tests/` directory (includes real examples)
- **Example files**: `../../examples/` directory  
- **Clean workspace**: All generated files removed with `--clean` flag
